				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13930240</guid>
				<title>Lord Blackwood Presents: A True Account of the Events of 1666</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13930240/lord-blackwood-presents:a-true-account-of-the-events-of-1666</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 13 Dec 2020 11:15:47 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Smapti</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>362048</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It's been a long time since I've felt like writing Lord Blackwood, or anything, or even reading the latest on the site for that matter. This has been percolating in my head for the last few weeks, though, partially inspired by current events and partially by ideas I've had floating around in my head for awhile now, and over the past few days I've felt the urge to get it out of my skull and share it with the world.</p> <p>Merry Christmas and I hope you enjoy.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13930143</guid>
				<title>Black Autumn IV: Nothing to Fear Hub</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13930143/black-autumn-iv:nothing-to-fear-hub</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 13 Dec 2020 09:25:19 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Ihp</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1267048</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Only a whole two months after I started putting this series up on the site, it <em>finally</em> has a hub. I'll link all of the tales to the hub when I can (probably tomorrow) but it's nice to have this up.</p> <p>I'm not gonna lie. This is tough for me to write&#8212; between the stress of my job and the chaos of the whole rest of the year, I've been on the verge of a nervous breakdown for a good two months. But when I actually <em>had</em> a breakdown, something in my brain became unstuck, and I'm finding it easier to write again. Yay?</p> <p>I <em>will</em> finish this, if it kills me. Thanks to everyone who's supported this so far.</p> <p>Unless copyright law has gone completely topsy-turvy, both the Bible and Antigonish are in the public domain.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
